            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 85-year-old male admitted on 04/09/1992 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without new consolidation. Blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Full blood count and inflammatory markers were obtained. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement in spirometric parameters and oxygen saturation. He is discharged in a stable condition and I would recommend close outpatient follow-up with optimisation of his inhaled maintenance therapy and pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
